---
description: graphify knowledge graph context
alwaysApply: true
---

This project has a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/` built from `knowledge/obsidian/` (Nova decisions, strategies, courses index, memory router).

- For questions about Nova decisions, strategy links, IBKR/Alpaca choices, Gap and Go, Nova OS phases, or how vault notes relate: when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists, first run `graphify query "<question>"` (or `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` / `graphify explain "<concept>"`). These return a scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than `GRAPH_REPORT.md` or raw vault greps.
- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading every Obsidian note
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review or when query/path/explain do not surface enough context
- Graphify complements (does not replace) Pinecone course recall and Obsidian source notes — see `knowledge/obsidian/00-System/Graphify-Knowledge-Graph.md`
- After editing notes under `knowledge/obsidian/`, rebuild with `/graphify knowledge/obsidian --update --wiki` (semantic; uses the assistant). Do not use AST-only `graphify update` for Markdown-only vault changes — that path is for code
- Optional later: `/graphify . --wiki` to add the full codebase into a separate or merged graph
